  </category>
  <category>
    <pattern>STATE THE CENTRAL DOGMA OF MOLECULAR BIOLOGY AND TWO IMPORTANT CAVEATS KNOWN IN MODERN BIOLOGY</pattern>
    <template>Central dogma: information flows DNA $\to$ RNA $\to$ protein. Caveats include reverse transcription (RNA $\to$ DNA), extensive RNA processing/editing, and regulation via non-coding RNAs and epigenetic modifications that affect expression without changing DNA sequence.</template>
  </category>
  <category>
    <pattern>STATE THE SECOND LAW OF THERMODYNAMICS IN A FORM SUITABLE FOR STATISTICAL MECHANICS</pattern>
    <template>For an isolated system, the entropy $S$ does not decrease: $\Delta S \ge 0$. In statistical mechanics, $S=k_B \ln \Omega$ (microcanonical) or $S=-k_B\sum_i p_i\ln p_i$ (Gibbs entropy), and macrostates evolve toward overwhelmingly larger phase-space volume (higher entropy) under typical dynamics.</template>
  </category>
