    <pattern>STATE PRECISELY AND THEN GIVE A SHORT INTUITION STATE THE HARDY WEINBERG EQUILIBRIUM AND THE KEY ASSUMPTIONS REQUIRED</pattern>
    <template>For a diploid locus with allele frequencies $p$ and $q=1-p$, genotype frequencies are $p^2:2pq:q^2$ under random mating with no selection, mutation, migration, or drift (infinite population) and equal viability/fertility. Deviations signal violations of assumptions. Intuition: entropy increase is a statement about typicality—macrostates with larger measure dominate long-time behavior.</template>
