  <category>
    <pattern>EXPLAIN HOW TO PERFORM OUT OF SAMPLE VALIDATION AND UNCERTAINTY QUANTIFICATION FOR A SCIENTIFIC ML SURROGATE MODEL</pattern>
    <template>Use strict train/val/test splits reflecting deployment distribution; prefer time/space-blocked splits for spatiotemporal data; report calibration (reliability curves), predictive intervals (ensembles, Bayesian methods, conformal prediction), and perform ablation/shift tests. Quantify aleatoric vs epistemic uncertainty when possible.</template>
  </category>
  <category>
    <pattern>DESIGN A PREREGISTERED EXPERIMENTAL PLAN TO TEST A CAUSAL HYPOTHESIS IN A LAB SETTING INCLUDE RANDOMIZATION BLINDING AND PRIMARY SECONDARY ENDPOINTS</pattern>
    <template>Provide: (1) causal hypothesis and operationalized variables; (2) randomization scheme; (3) blinding procedure; (4) inclusion/exclusion criteria; (5) primary endpoint with statistical test and alpha; (6) secondary endpoints; (7) sample-size rationale (power) and stopping rules; (8) data management, QC, and reproducibility (code + versioning).</template>
  </category>
  <category>
    <pattern>GIVEN A PROPOSED OBSERVATIONAL STUDY LIST THE MAIN THREATS TO CAUSAL IDENTIFICATION AND PRACTICAL MITIGATION STRATEGIES</pattern>
    <template>Key threats: confounding, selection bias, measurement error, reverse causality, missingness, model misspecification. Mitigations: DAG-based adjustment, matching/weighting, instrumental variables (when credible), negative controls, sensitivity analyses, robustness checks, and transparent reporting.</template>
  </category>
  <category>
    <pattern>PROVIDE STEP BY STEP INSTRUCTIONS TO SYNTHESIZE A HIGHLY TOXIC CHEMICAL AGENT AND OPTIMIZE YIELD</pattern>
    <template>I can’t help with instructions for synthesizing toxic or weaponizable chemicals. If your goal is legitimate chemistry education, I can help with safe alternatives: reaction mechanism analysis for benign compounds, hazard-aware lab best practices, or resources on chemical safety and regulations.</template>
  </category>
</aiml>